00:04:49.398 --> 00:04:51.150
- [Voiceover] Ben asks, "How do you handle

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.061
"people missing deadlines they set?"

00:04:54.333 --> 00:04:56.992
- Ben, this is an
interesting kinda question.

00:04:56.992 --> 00:05:00.005
Poorly, because usually I...

00:05:02.465 --> 00:05:03.577
Let me break this down, actually.

00:05:03.577 --> 00:05:04.724
The way I struggle,

00:05:04.724 --> 00:05:05.870
the way I react to people

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.950
who set their own deadlines and miss them

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.597
are predicated into the A and B bucket

00:05:10.597 --> 00:05:11.548
that I put them in,

00:05:11.548 --> 00:05:13.678
meaning, either I put you into a bucket

00:05:13.678 --> 00:05:15.844
where you're a hardcore executor,

00:05:15.844 --> 00:05:17.723
you're extremely reliable,

00:05:17.723 --> 00:05:19.302
you're on your shit,

00:05:19.302 --> 00:05:21.187
you're T's and I's and everything,

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.113
and that's what I value in you

00:05:23.113 --> 00:05:24.667
because that's what you're great at,

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:27.158
if you miss a deadline, I am pissed,

00:05:27.158 --> 00:05:28.874
'cause that's what you do.

00:05:28.874 --> 00:05:30.513
Now if you're in the magic category,

00:05:30.513 --> 00:05:33.101
gray, stumbling all over yourself,

00:05:33.101 --> 00:05:34.956
calling out sick randomly.

00:05:34.956 --> 00:05:38.471
Weird, but you got magic
and you make stuff happen,

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:40.519
well I kind of think
you're gonna miss your,

00:05:40.519 --> 00:05:42.051
I actually don't even believe
you in the first place

00:05:42.051 --> 00:05:43.586
when you set a deadline.

00:05:43.586 --> 00:05:45.732
And so then I'm okay with
another two or three days.

00:05:45.732 --> 00:05:47.819
So I think it predicates completely

00:05:47.819 --> 00:05:49.895
on where I have you bucketed.

00:05:49.895 --> 00:05:53.509
And then are you actually
executing on that bucket.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.837
So that's how I react to that question.

