00:06:07.079 --> 00:06:08.873
- [Voiceover] Cameron asks,
"What are your thoughts

00:06:08.873 --> 00:06:11.369
"on 3D printing technology
and the potential

00:06:11.369 --> 00:06:13.986
"to integrate with social media?"

00:06:14.235 --> 00:06:16.304
- I'm a big fan of 3D printing.

00:06:16.304 --> 00:06:18.313
I think if you play it out at scale,

00:06:18.313 --> 00:06:19.584
3D printing is one of the most

00:06:19.584 --> 00:06:21.234
disruptive things going on

00:06:21.234 --> 00:06:23.084
that I think a lotta people talked about

00:06:23.084 --> 00:06:25.228
and it's not the hot topic right now,

00:06:25.228 --> 00:06:28.294
which makes me feel like in 2019, 2022,

00:06:28.294 --> 00:06:30.133
it's gonna pop and everybody's
gonna be like, "What?"

00:06:30.133 --> 00:06:31.646
It's kinda like the
Internet itself, right?

00:06:31.646 --> 00:06:33.887
After the dot com bubble burst

00:06:33.887 --> 00:06:36.186
in '01 on Wall Street,

00:06:36.186 --> 00:06:38.108
people kind of didn't realize

00:06:38.108 --> 00:06:39.954
the Internet was only growing

00:06:39.954 --> 00:06:41.146
and would really be a factor.

00:06:41.146 --> 00:06:42.514
Same thing with 3D printing.

00:06:42.514 --> 00:06:43.784
It got a lotta pizzazz.

00:06:43.784 --> 00:06:45.703
Now it's a kind of soft period.

00:06:45.703 --> 00:06:46.275
Everyone's talkin' about the

00:06:46.275 --> 00:06:47.762
Ubers and the Airbnb's.

00:06:47.762 --> 00:06:49.380
I think it's gonna really rear its head

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.611
in five to seven years.

00:06:51.938 --> 00:06:53.247
How it integrates into social

00:06:53.247 --> 00:06:54.834
is not interesting.

00:06:54.834 --> 00:06:56.285
I'm not trying to be disrespectful.

00:06:56.285 --> 00:06:57.222
I don't think that's interesting.

00:06:57.222 --> 00:06:58.374
I think what's interesting is

00:06:58.374 --> 00:07:00.702
if you sell a physical good,

00:07:00.702 --> 00:07:03.167
between five and 100 dollars,

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:05.126
I think you have real disruption coming up

00:07:05.126 --> 00:07:07.444
in five, 10, 15, 20 years.

00:07:07.444 --> 00:07:11.055
Like, nobody's buying a
screwdriver in 15 years.

00:07:11.055 --> 00:07:12.197
You're making one.

00:07:12.197 --> 00:07:14.449
And that's intense.

00:07:14.449 --> 00:07:16.005
And then 3D printing gets into

00:07:16.005 --> 00:07:17.033
a real intense place,

00:07:17.033 --> 00:07:19.570
including people arguing about gun control

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:20.369
in a world where people can be

00:07:20.369 --> 00:07:22.350
printing guns in their home.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:23.696
Like, who gives a shit about

00:07:23.696 --> 00:07:25.184
gun shows and permits.

00:07:25.184 --> 00:07:26.409
I'm printing it in my basement.

00:07:26.409 --> 00:07:28.275
So society will evolve.

00:07:28.275 --> 00:07:29.758
We will always adjust.

00:07:29.758 --> 00:07:30.762
You go show somebody

00:07:30.762 --> 00:07:32.017
who lived 150 years ago

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:33.447
all the intensity we deal with,

00:07:33.447 --> 00:07:34.102
they would have thought

00:07:34.102 --> 00:07:36.087
that we woulda killed
ourselves off by now.

00:07:36.087 --> 00:07:38.402
Humans have a funny way to adjust.

00:07:38.402 --> 00:07:40.223
I'm in on team human.

00:07:40.223 --> 00:07:41.407
But don't get it twisted.

00:07:41.407 --> 00:07:44.319
3D printing is a massive disrupter.

00:07:44.319 --> 00:07:45.269
And over the next two decades,

00:07:45.269 --> 00:07:47.656
will rear it's head for all of us.

